      },
      "body": "Fixes #45517\r\n\r\n## Motivation\r\nFlashInfer softmax can return q slightly > 1.0 (max 1.0000068) on near-one-hot\r\nrows. The accept kernel unconditionally rejects q outside (0, 1], so the DSpark\r\naccept length collapses at certain temperatures (e.g. 1.75 at T=0.3).\r\n\r\n## Modifications\r\nIn `softmax_temp_flashinfer`, clamp the output to `max=1.0` (in-place on the\r\nfresh FlashInfer tensor; upper bound only).\r\n\r\n## Verification\r\n- Switching only SoftmaxTemp to triton (same effect as clamping) restores accept\r\n  length: T=0.05~1.2 all 7.5~7.6; business benchmark 1.75 -> 6.08.\r\n- Distribution change is at most ~7e-6 per element.\r\n\r\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:no_entry_sign: [Run #40392630210](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40392630210)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40392630111](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40392630111)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40392629872](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40392629872)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
      "changedFiles": 1,
      "comments": {
        "nodes": [
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "LevyJeng"
            },
            "body": "Hi @Qiaolin-Yu  , thanks for taking this one.\r\n\r\nCI is currently blocked at `pr-gate` only because the PR is missing the `run-ci`\r\nlabel (no tests actually ran). Could you help trigger it with `/tag-and-rerun-ci`?\r\n\r\nSummary for review: this is a one-line numerical fix. FlashInfer softmax can return\r\nq slightly > 1.0 (max 1.0000068) on near-one-hot rows, and the accept kernel\r\nunconditionally rejects q outside (0, 1]. Clamping restores DSpark accept length\r\nfrom 1.75 to 6.08 on our workload. Details and controlled experiments are in #45517.\r\n",
            "createdAt": "2026-10-22T05:55:18Z",
            "databaseId": 6333846411,
            "updatedAt": "2026-10-22T05:55:18Z",
            "url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/45518#issuecomment-6333846411"
          },
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "rohitg00"
            },
            "body": "#45517 is the same bug as #42568: `speculative_sampling_classic_kernel` rejects any q > 1.0, and `chain_speculative_sampling_triton` is also called from `eagle_utils.py` and `uno_utils.py`, not only from DSpark. #45819 fixes that guard in `reject_sampling.py`; the two changes touch different files and do not conflict.\n",
